  "body": "Per the thread at https://lists.w3.org/Archives/Public/public-web-bluetooth/2016Mar/0007.html, we'd like to have websites treat peripherals as if they're not bonded. That means that sites will need to re-discover services, characteristics, and descriptors after disconnecting, and they'll need to re-subscribe to notifications when they re-connect (#220), and might miss some that are fired between the connection and the re-subscription.\n",
